
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Card payments — BNCTL / Mastercard acquiring
#
# Leave EVERY value below blank and card payment simply does not appear at
# checkout; the existing manual methods (cash, bank transfer, wallet, fiar)
# keep working exactly as before. Nothing here is required to run the store.
#
# >>> Before switching this on, get BNCTL's merchant integration pack and
# >>> confirm the values against it. The adapter in
# >>> src/lib/payments/providers/mpgs.ts is written against the Mastercard
# >>> Payment Gateway Services REST API, which is the usual shape for a bank
# >>> acquiring on the Mastercard network -- but it has NOT been verified
# >>> against BNCTL's own documentation.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Which adapter to use. Only "bnctl" ships today.
# PAYMENT_PROVIDER=bnctl

# Gateway REST host, from BNCTL. No trailing slash.
# MPGS_HOST=https://bnctl.gateway.mastercard.com
# MPGS_MERCHANT_ID=
# MPGS_API_PASSWORD=
# MPGS_API_VERSION=100

# Shared secret used to verify webhook signatures (HMAC-SHA256 over the raw
# body). Without it the webhook endpoint refuses every request -- which is
# the correct default: an unverified webhook that marks orders paid is a
# "mark any order paid" endpoint for anyone who finds the URL.
# MPGS_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
# MPGS_SIGNATURE_HEADER=x-notification-signature

# The gateway's browser-facing origin, added to the Content-Security-Policy
# so the hosted payment page is allowed to load. Usually the same host as
# MPGS_HOST. Without this the payment page is blocked by CSP and the only
# clue is a browser console message your buyer will never read.
# PAYMENT_GATEWAY_ORIGIN=https://bnctl.gateway.mastercard.com

# Shown as the merchant name on the hosted payment page.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_STORE_NAME=Loja AIAI

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Order notifications — WhatsApp message to the buyer, with a one-tap
# tracking link, when their order is placed and each time it moves.
#
# LEAVE EVERYTHING BELOW BLANK AND THE FEATURE STILL WORKS. With no provider
# configured the store queues every message and shows the admin a one-tap
# "Send on WhatsApp" button on the order page (and a queue at
# /admin/notifications). That needs no Meta account and costs nothing --
# it just needs a human to press send.
#
# Filling these in makes the same messages send themselves. Nothing else
# changes: same text, same links, same outbox.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# From Meta -> WhatsApp -> API Setup. The ID of the number messages are sent
# FROM (not the number itself).
# WHATSAPP_PHONE_NUMBER_ID=

# A permanent System User access token. The temporary one shown during setup
# expires in 24 hours and will strand your notifications overnight.
# WHATSAPP_ACCESS_TOKEN=

# >>> Read this before going live <<<
# WhatsApp does NOT allow free-form text to someone who has not messaged your
# business in the last 24 hours. Outside that window only a pre-approved
# TEMPLATE is delivered.
#
#   Left blank      -> plain text. Fine for the order-confirmation message
#                      minutes after checkout; an "out for delivery" the next
#                      morning will be refused, and the message stays in the
#                      admin queue to be sent by hand.
#   Set             -> template message. Submit a template to Meta whose body
#                      is a single {{1}} parameter, wait for approval, then
#                      put its name here.
# WHATSAPP_TEMPLATE_NAME=
# WHATSAPP_TEMPLATE_LANG=en

# Required for the tracking links to be tappable — they go into a chat
# message, where a relative path is just text. Without it notifications are
# skipped rather than sent with a broken link.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://your-domain.tl

# Already required for admin login; the tracking links are signed with it too,
# so changing it invalidates every link already sitting in buyers' phones.
# SESSION_SECRET=
